Allow NOMMU regions which start at the same address.

Direct character device mappings may overlap other regions; do_mmap()
says so where it searches for shareable regions. A /dev/mem mapping at
another region's start address, such as a page the process has already
mapped, nevertheless hit BUG() in add_nommu_region() and panicked.
Order regions with equal starts by their own addresses instead.

diff --git a/mm/nommu.c b/mm/nommu.c
--- a/mm/nommu.c
+++ b/mm/nommu.c
@@ -496,8 +496,11 @@
 			p = &(*p)->rb_right;
 		else if (pregion == region)
 			return;
+		/* Direct device mappings may alias another region's start. */
+		else if (region < pregion)
+			p = &(*p)->rb_left;
 		else
-			BUG();
+			p = &(*p)->rb_right;
 	}
 
 	rb_link_node(&region->vm_rb, parent, p);
